# Wave W17-O (Route 114): impact turf — crater-field grass: warm dry green with the sky’s old arguments ground into it — grey-tan stone-dust flecks scattered through the sward where the craters weather out (design: calm speckled grass across a crater-scarred hillside, warm earthy palette). Route 114’s own ground — dustier than the Pass’s worn ledge grass and split from Route 113’s ash turf by the dust’s nature: this is STONE dust, warm and gritty, not grey ash fall.
